38. Procedure with OUT parameter — total number of orders

Now we're introducing OUT.

DELIMITER //

CREATE PROCEDURE total_orders(OUT p_total INT)
BEGIN
    SELECT COUNT(*)
    INTO p_total
    FROM sales_orders;
END //

DELIMITER ;
What happens?

This:

SELECT COUNT(*)
INTO p_total

puts the count into the OUT parameter.

39. Call Q38 and display returned value

First create a session variable:

SET @total = 0;

Call the procedure:

CALL total_orders(@total);

Display the result:

SELECT @total AS total_orders;
Important difference

@total is a session variable.

The procedure puts its result into it.

